  "title": "Understanding Developmental Stages",
  "content": "Children grow in predictable patterns, but each child develops at their own pace. Understanding developmental stages helps parents set realistic expectations and respond with patience. Development includes emotional, social, physical, and cognitive growth, and each area influences the others.\n\nWhen parents understand what is typical for a child’s age, they are less likely to misinterpret behaviour as defiance or disrespect. For example, toddlers are not capable of long attention spans, and teenagers naturally seek independence. These behaviours are developmental, not personal.\n\nThis lesson explores how children’s brains develop and how parents can support growth by offering guidance that matches their child’s abilities. When expectations align with development, conflict decreases and connection increases.",
